  m_text: 'Initially introduced by Hokkien-speaking Chinese migrants and traders
    who introduced noodles to the Philippine islands. The dish evolved with local
    ingredients and techniques and is a common everyday meal. Pancit carries a superstition
    still observed today; not to cut the noodles as long strands are believed to
    symbolise a long life which is why this dish is popular at Filipino birthdays. '
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
